# Tasks: EXECUTION-CONTRACT

Purpose:
  Define the per-task execution contract that the AI must establish
  before beginning autonomous work. The contract declares the goal,
  allowed scope, forbidden actions, approval requirements, budgets,
  and autonomy level. The AI then operates strictly within this contract.

Owns:
  Execution contract schema
  Plan immutability vs evolution
  Execution trace format
  Execution summary format

Contract:

  schema:
    task_id: string (e.g. TASK-1023)
    goal: string (single primary objective)
    allowed: [paths or scopes]
    allowed_actions: [code, tests, docs, config, refactor, research]
    forbidden: [actions, paths, or changes]
    approval_required: [trigger conditions needing human approval]
    max_iterations: integer
    max_failure_budget: integer (severity-weighted)
    autonomy: L0 | L1 | L2 | L3 | L4 | L5
    plan_version: integer (starts at 1)
    state: current task state (bax TASK-STATE-MACHINE.sdd)

  Example:
    TASK EXECUTION CONTRACT
    task_id: TASK-1023
    goal:
      implement refund
    allowed:
      backend/payment
    allowed_actions:
      code
      tests
      docs
    forbidden:
      DB destructive migration
    approval_required:
      public API change
    max_iterations: 8
    max_failure_budget: 5
    autonomy: L3
    plan_version: 1
    state: PLANNING

PlanEvolution:

  principle: plan is NOT immutable — it evolves with new evidence
  rule: plan changes MUST be recorded with reason and evidence
  rule: reverting a plan counts as plan_reverted (+20 LOOP_SCORE)
  rule: plan evolution triggered by new evidence is encouraged
  rule: plan thrashing (flip-flop without new evidence) triggers
        loop protection

  PlanChangeLog:
    PLAN CHANGE
    task_id: TASK-1023
    from:
      direct event publish
    to:
      transactional outbox
    reason:
      discovered existing project decision @decision.outbox-for-provider-events
    evidence:
      - @../references/architecture/event-driven.sdd
      - prior task TASK-1018 found deadlock with direct publish

ExecutionTrace:

  format:
    #01 <action> <result>
    #02 <action> <result>
    ...

  rules:
    [ET1] Every significant action gets a trace entry.
    [ET2] Failure entries MUST classify the failure (bax
          FAILURE-CLASSIFICATION.sdd).
    [ET3] Trace entries MUST be numbered sequentially per task.
    [ET4] Trace is runtime-only — compressed into knowledge at task end.

  Example:
    #01 Discover
    #02 Load @payment.idempotency
    #03 Plan transaction
    #04 Implement
    #05 Test
    #06 Failure: ENVIRONMENT_FAILURE — missing provider credentials
    #07 Analyze
    #08 Change locking order
    #09 Test
    #10 Pass
    #11 Review
    #12 Complete

ExecutionSummary:

  format:
    TASK-<ID> SUMMARY
    Goal: <goal>
    Result: completed | blocked | escalated | partially_completed
    Iterations: <n>
    Tests: <count> passed
    Architecture: valid | invalid
    New knowledge: @skill.* or @decision.* (or none)
    Important decision: @decision.* (or none)
    Failed approach: <description> (or none)

  rules:
    [ES1] Summary is the persistent artifact from runtime trace.
    [ES2] Runtime trace (100+ events) collapses into: important
          decisions + new skills + failed approaches.
    [ES3] Summary is human-readable and machine-parseable.

Rules:

  [EC1] AI MUST establish the execution contract before starting a task.
  [EC2] AI MUST NOT perform actions outside `allowed_actions`.
  [EC3] AI MUST NOT modify files outside `allowed` scope.
  [EC4] AI MUST stop immediately when a `forbidden` action is required
        to meet the goal — this is a CONSTRAINT_FAILURE.
  [EC5] AI MUST request human approval before any action matching
        `approval_required`.
  [EC6] `max_iterations` and `max_failure_budget` are enforced by
        LOOP-PROTECTION.sdd.
  [EC7] `autonomy` level determines what the AI can do without approval
        (bax AUTONOMY-POLICY.sdd).
  [EC8] Plan changes MUST record the reason — plan thrashing is forbidden.
  [EC9] Every task MUST produce an execution summary at completion.
  [EC10] The contract is the boundary — crossing it without approval
         is a violation.

Navigation:

  StateMachine: @TASK-STATE-MACHINE.sdd
  LoopProtection: @LOOP-PROTECTION.sdd
  FailureClassification: @FAILURE-CLASSIFICATION.sdd
  AutonomyPolicy: @AUTONOMY-POLICY.sdd
  DoneProof: @DONE-PROOF.sdd
  PartialDone: @PARTIAL-DONE.sdd
  TasksIndex: @INDEX.sdd

